1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:07,060
Hey. Hey. So how was Joan?
瓊安好不好？

3
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,720
Broke up with her. Oh, why?
跟她分手了 為什麼？

4
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,140
Don't tell me. Because of the big nostril thing?
別告訴我 因為鼻孔太大？

5
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:18,780
They were huge. When she sneezed, bats flew out of them
真的超大！ 她打噴嚏時 會有蝙蝠飛出來

6
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:23,940
Oh, come on. They were not that huge. I'm telling you, she leaned back. I could
沒那麼大

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:28,820
see her brain. How many perfectly fine women are you going

8
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:33,760
to reject over the most superficial, insignificant... Oh, hold it, hold it. I mean, I got to side

9
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,240
with Chandler on this one. When I first moved to the city, I went out a couple times with
我剛搬到這裡時 與一個女孩交往

10
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:42,360
this girl. Really hot, great kisser, but she had the biggest Adam's apple
非常熱情，很會接吻… 但是她的喉結非常大粒！

11
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:47,820
Drove me nuts. You or me?
真是讓我受不了

12
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:52,660
I got it. Joey, women don't have Adam's apples
喬伊，女人沒有喉結

13
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:05,220
You guys are messing with me, right? Yes, we are
你們是在騙我，對不對？

14
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,980
That was a good one. For a second there, I was like, whoa

15
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:03,160
You name one woman that you broke up with for an actual, real reason
你與哪個女友分手 是因為正當的理由？

16
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:07,700
Maureen Razzillo. Because she doesn't hate Yanni is not a real
因為她不討厭音樂家雅尼 這不是個正當的理由

17
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:14,560
reason. Hello, Mr. Heckles
嗨，哈克先生

18
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,880
You're doing it again. We're not doing anything
你們又來了 我們什麼都沒做

19
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:25,840
You're stomping. It's disturbing my birds. You don't have birds
你們腳步聲太響 嚇到了我的鳥兒 你沒有養鳥

20
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:31,780
I could have birds. Okay, Mr. Heckles, we'll try to keep it down
我可以養鳥 我們會小聲一點

21
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:35,180
Thank you. I'm going to rejoin my dinner party
謝謝 我要回去繼續宴客了

22
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:43,200
All right, bye-bye. Okay, Janice. Janice, you got to give me Janice
好，再見 對了，珍妮絲

23
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:45,820
That wasn't about being picky. Yeah, we'll give you Janice
我們同意你與珍妮絲分手

24
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:50,420
I miss Janice, though. Hello, Chandler Bing
但我蠻想珍妮絲的 嗨，錢德寶！

25
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:59,060
Oh, my God. Oh, Chandler, now
喔，我的天！ 喔，錢德！

26
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:03,940
Yeah. That's it
對了

27
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:15,720
Yeah, faster. Stop with the broom
別用掃把了！ 我們沒有製造噪音！

28
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:28,500
We're not making noise. We won
我們贏了

29
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:35,420
We did it. Mr. Heckles
我們勝利了！ 哈克先生！

30
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:41,820
How did this happen? He must have been sweeping
怎麼發生的？ 他大概在掃地

31
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:48,900
They found a broom in his hand. That's terrible
他們發現他抓著一把掃把

32
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,260
I know. I was sweeping yesterday
昨天我也在掃地

33
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:56,540
Could have been me. You were sweeping

34
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,680
You never know. Never know
世事難料

35
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,300
Okay. It's very faint, but I can still sense him
很微弱 但我還可以感覺他在大樓裡

36
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:10,420
in the building. Go into the light, Mr. Heckles
進入光芒中，哈克先生！

37
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:18,420
Okay, Phoebe. I'm sorry, but sometimes they need help
好了，菲比 對不起 有時候他們需要幫助

38
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,340
Here we go. That's fine
又來了

39
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:27,060
Go ahead and scoff. You know, there are a lot of things out there
我不相信很多事情…

40
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,420
that I don't believe in, but that doesn't mean they're not true
但這不表示就不是真的

41
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:35,060
Such as? Like crop circles or the Bermuda Triangle
譬如什麼事？

42
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:37,320
or evolution. Whoa, whoa, whoa

43
00:04:40,140 --> 00:04:43,660
You don't believe in evolution? No, not really
不真的相信 你不相信進化論？

44
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:49,380
You don't believe in evolution? I don't know
你不相信進化論？

45
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:53,940
It's just, you know, monkeys, Darwin. You know, it's a nice story
猴子，達爾文，很好的故事 我只是覺得有點太簡單

46
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:59,980
I just think it's a little too easy. Too easy?
太簡單？太…

47
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:05,320
Too... The process of every living thing on this planet
這個星球上的一切生物 經過數千萬年…

48
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:08,740
evolving over millions of years from single-celled organisms
從單細胞微生物進化而成 而你說太簡單？

49
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:12,520
is too easy? Yeah, I just don't buy it
對，我不太相信

50
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:17,740
Excuse me. Evolution is not for you to buy, Phoebe
對不起 進化論不是信不信由你，菲比

51
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:22,440
Evolution is scientific fact, like the air we breathe
進化論是科學事實 就像我們呼吸的空氣…

52
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:24,940
like gravity. Oh, okay

53
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:32,920
Don't get me started on gravity. You, uh, you don't believe in gravity?
別跟我提起地心引力 你不相信地心引力？

54
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:37,780
Well, it's not so much that, you know, like I don't believe in it
倒不是相不相信的問題

55
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:40,980
You know, it's just, I don't know. Lately, I get the feeling that
最近我感覺到…

56
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:44,480
I'm not so much being pulled down as I am being pushed
我不是被吸住，而是被壓著 被壓著…

57
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:53,280
Uh-oh, it's Isaac Newton and he's pissed. Quick, Pheebs, up on the ceiling

58
00:05:56,020 --> 00:05:59,220
Oh, there she is. And over there, that's the other one
她在那邊，那裡還有另一個

59
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:03,140
This is Mr. Buddy Boyle, Heckle's attorney. He'd like to talk to you
這是伯弟杜爾 哈克的律師 他想跟你們談談

60
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:06,880
Okay, what can we do for you? All right, kids, here's the deal
有何貴幹？ 好了，孩子們 事情是這樣的

61
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:12,260
According to my client's will, he wants to leave all his earthly possessions
他要把他所有財產…

62
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:17,080
to the, uh, noisy girls in the apartment above mine

63
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:21,740
Oh! But what about his family? He didn't have any
他的家人呢？ 他沒有家人

64
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:25,920
Whoa. Okay, so let's talk money
好，讓我們看看有多少錢

65
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:31,800
All right, there was none. Now, let's talk signing
好，沒有半毛錢 現在，我們來簽字

66
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,960
You be noisy girl number one, you be noisy girl number two
你是一號吵鬧女孩 你是二號吵鬧女孩

67
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:39,540
I can't believe that this whole time we thought he hated us
我真不相信 我們一直以為他討厭我們

68
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:45,180
I mean, isn't it amazing how much you can touch someone's life without even knowing it?
真是不可思議 我們能如此感動其他人… 而自己卻不知道？

69
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:50,080
Would you look at this dump? He hated us. This was his final revenge
看看這個豬窩？！ 他痛恨我們！ 這是他最終的報復！

70
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:52,440
Ever seen so much crap?
我從來沒看過這麼多廢物！

71
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:55,620
Actually, I think this apartment sullies the good name of crap
我覺得這間公寓 侮辱了廢物的美名

72
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:58,580
Ooh, check this out
看看這個

73
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,780
Can I have this?
這個能給我嗎？

74
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,520
How can you not believe in evolution?
你怎麼能不相信進化論？

75
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:10,600
I don't know. Just, uh, look at this funky shirt
我不知道，就是不相信 看看這條怪襯衫！

76
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:14,740
Pheebs, I've studied evolution my entire adult life, okay?
菲比 我整個成年都在研究進化論

77
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:18,100
And I can tell you, we have collected fossils from all over the world

78
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:22,060
that actually show the evolution of different species, okay?
能夠證明不同物種的進化論

79
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:27,480
I mean, you can literally see them evolving through time
可以真正看到它們… 透過時間進化

80
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:31,740
Really? You can actually see it?
真的？可以看得到？

81
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:36,260
You bet. In the U.S., China, Africa, all over
千真萬確！在美國 中國，非洲，全世界！

82
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,340
See, I didn't know that
這我不知道

83
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:40,800
Well, there you go
這就是吧

84
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:45,700
Huh. So now, the real question is
所以真的問題是 誰把化石放在那裡？為什麼？

85
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,440
who put those fossils there and why?
所以真的問題是 誰把化石放在那裡？為什麼？

86
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:55,320
Hey, look at this. My big book of grievances
看看這個！ 我的痛苦之書

87
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,400
Hey, there's me
嘿，這是我！

88
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:03,400
April 17th. Excessive noise
四月十七日，噪音過度…

89
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,900
Italian guy comes home with a date
意大利佬帶了女伴回家

90
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:09,020
Hey, Chandler, look. You're in here, too
你也在裡面

91
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,580
April 18th. Excessive noise
四月十八日，噪音過度…

92
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,720
Italian guy's gay roommate brings home dry cleaning
意大利佬帶了女伴回家

93
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,600
Well, that's excellent
真是太好了

94
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:27,480
Monica, Monica, look at this lamp
看看這盞燈

95
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:29,660
Is this tacky or what? We have to have this
真是夠俗了 我們一定要帶回去！

96
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:33,160
Uh, Rach, I think we have enough regular lamps
我們的好檯燈夠多了

97
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:38,320
What? Oh, come on. I mean, it's not like I'm asking for this girly clock or anything
要這個美女時鐘或什麼的

98
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:40,860
Which, by the way, I also think is really cool
但我覺得這個也很酷

99
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,880
Look, it doesn't go with any of my stuff
聽著，它與我的東西都不搭配

100
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:47,820
Well, what about my stuff? You don't have any stuff
那麼我的東西呢？ 你沒有任何東西

101
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:49,900
This'll be the start of my stuff

102
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:51,540
Mmm, no

103
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:55,000
You still think of it as your apartment, don't you?
你還是認為那是你的公寓 對不對？

104
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,680
Mmm, no. Yes, you do
對，你是這麼想

105
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:02,480
You think of it as your apartment, and I'm just someone who rents a room
你把它想成是你的公寓 我只是租了個房間

106
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:04,380
Mmm
你支支吾吾的時候 我會為我的新檯燈找個地方放

107
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:07,760
Okay, while you mmm on that for a while
你支支吾吾的時候 我會為我的新檯燈找個地方放

108
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,560
I'm gonna go find a place for my new lamp

109
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:16,500
Okay, peeps, see how I'm making these little toys move?

110
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:20,800
Opposable thumbs
可對立的拇指！

111
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:26,340
Without evolution, how do you explain opposable thumbs?
可對立的拇指！ 沒有進化論 怎麼發展出可對立的拇指？

112
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:31,580
Maybe the overlords needed them to steer their spacecrafts
也許外星主宰需要拇指 才能夠駕駛飛碟

113
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,400
Please tell me you're joking
請說你是在開玩笑

114
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:38,980
Look, can't we just say that you believe in something and I don't?
能不能說你相信進化論 而我不相信？

115
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:41,420
No, no. No, Pheebs, we can't, okay?
不行，菲比，不能這樣 為什麼不行？

116
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:44,800
Because it's like math. 1 plus 1 equals 2

117
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:48,000
I can't stand by and let you think that 1 plus 1

118
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,940
might equal 3 or 4 or yellow

119
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:55,540
Why not? No, what's that all about?
這是怎麼回事？ 你知道我怎麼想嗎？

120
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:59,680
What is this obsessive need you have to make everybody agree with you?
為什麼非得每個人都同意你？

121
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:02,360
You know what? I think maybe it's time
我想你也許應該好好檢視一下 羅斯這個生物了

122
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:05,440
you put Ross under the microscope
我想你也許應該好好檢視一下 羅斯這個生物了

123
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:12,400
Is there blood coming out of my ears?
我耳朵有沒有流血？

124
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:17,520
Check it out. Check it out. Heckles' high school yearbook
看看這個 哈克的高中同學錄

125
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:20,800
Wow, he looks so normal
他看起來好正常！

126
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,600
Yeah, he's even kind of cute
甚至有點可愛

127
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:25,840
Heckles, you cracked me up in science class
「哈克 你上科學課總是讓我捧腹大笑」

128
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,580
Heckles, you're the funniest kid in school
「哈克 你上科學課總是讓我捧腹大笑」 「你是全校最有趣的學生」

129
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:30,580
Funniest? Heckles? That's what it says
最有趣？哈克？ 上面是這樣寫的

130
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:34,100
Wow, Heckles was voted class clown, and so was I
哈克被選為班上的活寶 我也是

131
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,740
He was right. Would you listen to that?
他說得對！ 聽聽那個噪音？

132
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,520
I'd call that excessive
的確是很吵鬧

133
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:43,020
Whoa. What?
什麼？

134
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:46,360
Heckles played clarinet in band, and I played clarinet
哈克在樂隊演奏豎笛 我也是

135
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,000
And he was in the scale modelers club, and I was
他參加模型俱樂部 我也…

136
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,780
Well, there was no club, but I sure thought they were cool
雖然我的學校沒有俱樂部 但我覺得模型很酷

137
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,980
So, you're both dorks

138
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:57,920
Big deal
沒什麼值得大驚小怪

139
00:10:58,460 --> 00:11:00,720
I just think it's weird, you know? Heckles and me
我覺得很怪，哈克與我…

140
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,260
Heckles and me. Me. Me and Heckles
哈克與我，我… 我與哈克

141
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,160
Hey, would you knock it off?
喂，別吵好不好！

142
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:12,640
Bah!

143
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,540
Have you been here all night?
你整晚都在這裡？

144
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:33,300
Look at this. Pictures of all the women that Heckles went out with
看看這個

145
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:34,600
Look what he wrote on them
看看他在上面寫的 「薇安，太高大」

146
00:11:35,380 --> 00:11:36,460
Vivian, too tall
看看他在上面寫的 「薇安，太高大」

147
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:39,080
Madge, big gums
「瑪姬，牙齦太多」

148
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:42,480
Too loud. Too smart
「太大聲」

149
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:45,460
Makes noise when she eats. This is me
這就是我

150
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:47,020
This is what I do
這就是我的作法

151
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,120
I'm gonna end up alone, just like he did
我會像他一樣孤獨終老

152
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,740
Chandler, Heckles was a nutcase
哈克是個神經病

153
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,980
Our trains are on the same track, okay?
我們的人生道路方向一樣

154
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:59,600
Yeah, sure, I'm coming up 30 years behind him, but the stops are all the same
我比他晚了30年 但終點都是一樣

155
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:04,020
Bittertown. Aloneville. Hermit Junction
愁苦城… 孤獨鎮，隱士村！

156
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,080
Hey, you know what we gotta do?
我們應該離開這裡

157
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:10,460
We gotta get you outta here. Come on, I'll buy you breakfast. Let's go
我請你吃早餐

158
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:11,820
Well, what if I never find somebody?
要是我一直找不到伴侶？ 或更糟的，我已經找到了…

159
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:16,460
Or even worse, what if I already found her, but I dumped her because she pronounces it supposedly?
但我卻因為她說「厚許」 就甩了她？

160
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,580
Chandler, come on
錢德，好啦 你會找到對象的

161
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:21,080
You're gonna find somebody
錢德，好啦 你會找到對象的

162
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:23,320
How do you know that? How?
你怎麼知道？

163
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,220
I don't know. I'm just trying to help you out
我不知道 我只是想幫你下台

164
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:30,640
You'll see. You guys are all gonna go off and get married, and I'm gonna end up alone

165
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:32,740
Will you promise me something?
你能不能答應我一件事？

166
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:35,720
When you're married, will you invite me over for holidays?
你結婚後 過節時能不能請我去玩？

167
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,800
I mean, I don't know what we're gonna be doing
我不知道我們會怎麼樣

168
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:44,500
I mean, what if we're over at her folks' place?
要是我與妻子 到我岳父母那裡過節呢？

169
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:48,720
Yeah, I understand
我瞭解

170
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,480
You can come over and watch the Super Bowl
你可以過來看超級杯

171
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:56,920
Every year, all right?
每一年都來，怎麼樣？

172
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:59,240
You know what?
我不要像這樣子下場！

173
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:03,060
I'm not gonna end up like this. I'll see you, man
待會見，兄弟

174
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:08,900
Jeez

175
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,440
Supposedly

176
00:13:18,060 --> 00:13:18,660
Supposedly

177
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:23,200
Did they go to the zoo?
他們去動物園了嗎？

178
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:25,660
Supposedly

179
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,140
Supposedly

180
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:41,080
Hi. It's me
嗨，是我

181
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:45,320
Oh. My. God
我的天！

182
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:49,520
Janice? You called Janice?
珍妮絲？你打給珍妮絲？

183
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:54,260
Yes, Janice. Why is that so difficult for you to comprehend?
是的，珍妮絲

184
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,560
You remember Janice, right?
你還記得珍妮絲吧？

185
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,020
Yes. She was smart. She was pretty
是啊，她很聰明，很漂亮 而且很關心我

186
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,780
And she honestly cared about me
是啊，她很聰明，很漂亮 而且很關心我

187
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,500
Janice is my last chance to have somebody
珍妮絲是我的最後一個希望

188
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:07,700
Hello

189
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,180
Oh. My. God
喔，天啊！

190
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:18,600
Jeez. Look how fat she got
她真是胖了不少

191
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,080
Hey. It's everybody
嗨，大家都在這裡！ 嗨，珍妮絲

192
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:25,780
Janice, you're
珍妮絲，你…

193
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:27,680
Yes, I am
是的，我有了

194
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,140
Is it?

195
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:32,620
Is it yours? Ha! You wish, Chandler Bing
沒那麼好的事，錢德寶！

196
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:36,740
You are looking at a married lady now
我已經是少奶奶了

197
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:38,240
Oh
要我錯過看到你的表情？ 才不要！

198
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:41,340
Congratulations

199
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:46,400
Oh, sweetie. I'm sorry
甜心，真抱歉

200
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,260
I couldn't wait for you forever

201
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,200
You couldn't have told me about this over the phone?
你不能在電話上告訴我嗎？

202
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:53,860
And what? Miss the expression on your face?
要我錯過看到你的表情？ 才不要！

203
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:57,140
Oh, no. Janice likes to have her fun
珍妮絲喜歡樂子！

204
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:11,960
Hey, Rach. You know what we haven't played in a while?
你知道我們很久沒玩什麼嗎？

205
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:12,480
What?
要我錯過看到你的表情？ 才不要！

206
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:13,800
Hide the Lamp
藏起檯燈

207
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,140
Monica, let it go
摩妮卡，算了吧

208
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,280
Did you know I was allergic to shellfish?
你知道我對貝類過敏嗎？

209
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:23,900
Well, then, you'll just have to eat the other lamps
那麼你必須吃其他的檯燈

210
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:30,080
Uh-oh. It's Scary Scientist Man
可怕的科學家來了

211
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,640
Okay, Phoebe. This is it
菲比，這些就是了

212
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:38,920
In this briefcase, I carry actual scientific facts
在這個手提箱中 我帶來了真正的科學證據

213
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:41,760
A briefcase of facts, if you will
可算是整個提箱的證據

214
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:49,060
Some of these fossils are over 200 million years old
其中有些化石超過2億年老

215
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:50,660
Okay, look. Before you even start
我要先告訴你 我並不否定進化論

216
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,840
I'm not denying evolution, okay?

217
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:54,860
I'm just saying that it's one of the possibilities

218
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,860
It's the only possibility, Phoebe
進化論是唯一的可能

219
00:15:57,060 --> 00:16:00,500
Okay. Ross, could you just open your mind like this much?
羅斯 你能不能稍稍敞開心胸？

220
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,520
Okay? Now, wasn't there a time

221
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:06,720
when the brightest minds in the world believed that the Earth was flat?

222
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:09,640
And up until, like, what, 50 years ago

223
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:12,240
you all thought the atom was the smallest thing

224
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:16,020
until you split it open and this, like, whole mess of crap came out
後來科學家擊碎了原子 於是產生了各種玩意…

225
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,620
Now, are you telling me
難道你是如此自大…

226
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:22,300
that you are so unbelievably arrogant
難道你是如此自大…

227
00:16:22,300 --> 00:16:26,480
that you can't admit that there's a teeny tiny possibility
無法承認有一點點的可能…

228
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,780
that you could be wrong about this?
你們科學家也許會犯錯？

229
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:36,660
There might be
是有一點點…

230
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:39,940
a teeny
無法承認有一點點的可能…

231
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:42,500
tiny
無法承認有一點點的可能…

232
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:45,400
possibility
無法承認有一點點的可能…

233
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:49,580
I can't believe you caved
我真不相信你屈服了

234
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:52,820
What?
怎麼了？

235
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:55,760
You just abandoned your whole belief system

236
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,980
I mean, before, I didn't agree with you

237
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:01,420
but at least I respected you

238
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:05,320
How are you going to go into work tomorrow?

239
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:08,620
How are you going to face the other science guys?

240
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:10,760
How are you going to face yourself?

241
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,040
That was fun. So who's hungry?

242
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:31,180
I am
我餓了

243
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:44,900
Okay, all right

244
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,660
It was an accident, I swear
這是意外，我發誓

245
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:49,280
All right, I was putting on my jacket and the thing
我正在穿外套 檯燈就破了

246
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:50,820
and the lamp and it broke
我正在穿外套 檯燈就破了

247
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:54,240
Oh, please, Monica, you've always hated my lamp
拜託，摩妮卡！ 你痛恨我的檯燈！

248
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:56,120
And now, all of a sudden
突然間 它就奇跡似地破了？

249
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:59,020
it's just magically, it's just broken?
突然間 它就奇跡似地破了？

250
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:00,440
Phoebe, tell her
菲比，告訴她

251
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:03,240
Okay, I didn't see it because I was putting on my jacket
我沒看到 因為我正在穿外套

252
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:05,780
but I want to believe you
但我想要相信你

253
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,620
Hey, Chandler
嗨，錢德 摩妮卡打破了我的貝殼檯燈

254
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,880
Monica just broke my seashell lamp
嗨，錢德 摩妮卡打破了我的貝殼檯燈

255
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:16,860
Neat. I'm going to die alone
真好

256
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,020
Okay, you win
好，算你贏

257
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:25,400
Chandler, you are not going to die alone
錢德，你不會死得孤苦伶仃

258
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:27,880
Janice was my safety net, okay?
本來珍妮絲是我的安全保障

259
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:29,440
And now I have to get a snake
現在我必須去養一條蛇了

260
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,800
Uh-huh. Why is that?
為什麼？

261
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:35,440
If I'm going to be an old, lonely man

262
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:37,900
I'm going to need a thing, you know, a hook
有個依靠

263
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,500
Like that guy on the subway who eats his own face
就像地鐵上那個吃自己臉的人

264
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:43,860
So I figure I'll be Crazy Man with a Snake
我會成為 「養蛇的瘋老頭」

265
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,760
You know, Crazy Snake Man
養蛇瘋子

266
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:48,360
Then I'll get more snakes, call them my babies
然後我會養更多蛇 當成我的子女

267
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:50,620
kids won't walk past my place, they will run

268
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:52,360
Run away from Crazy Snake Man
養蛇瘋子

269
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:52,980
No, shop

270
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:59,920
You've got to get over this, okay?
你必須想開一點

271
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,980
You're not going to end up alone

272
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:03,440
Of course I am

273
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:07,580
I reject anyone who's crazy enough to actually go out with me
我甩掉了所有 笨得願意跟我交往的女孩

274
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,680
and then I bitch about the fact that there aren't any great women out there
然後我抱怨找不到好女孩

275
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:15,640
Chandler, you have just described
我們所交往的男人…

276
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:19,440
virtually every man that we have ever gone out with
就跟你所描述的一樣

277
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:20,100
Yeah

278
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:23,360
You are not a freak. You're a guy
你沒什麼問題 你只是個平常人

279
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:25,980
Yeah, honey, she's right
她說得對

280
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:27,420
I mean, you all do it

281
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:31,640
This one guy stopped seeing me because his cat didn't like me

282
00:19:31,860 --> 00:19:35,220
Or this guy dumped me because I fell asleep during Spinal Tap

283
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:37,320
You fell asleep during Spinal Tap?

284
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:40,800
Oh, oh, that Teddy-what's-his-name in high school

285
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:43,260
who stopped seeing you because he thought you were too fat

286
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:47,520
He told me it was because he didn't have time for me because of the play

287
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:49,920
That's what I said

288
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:55,240
Anyway, my point being, you are no different than the rest of them

289
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:57,200
Wait a minute, wait a minute. Yes, he is
等一下，等一下 他是不一樣

290
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:59,320
You are totally different
你其實很不一樣

291
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:00,520
In a bad way?
很糟糕嗎？

292
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:04,500
No, honey, in a wonderful way. You know what you want now
不，甜心，是很好的不一樣 現在你知道你要什麼了

293
00:20:04,940 --> 00:20:06,280
Most guys don't even have a clue
大多數男人根本不知道

294
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:10,620
You are ready to take risks. You're ready to be vulnerable and intimate with someone
你準備好接受風險了 準備好接受傷害，與人親近

295
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:12,280
Yeah, you're not going to end up alone
你不會孤苦伶仃的

296
00:20:12,280 --> 00:20:15,320
Chandler, you called Janice
你打電話給珍妮絲 這證明你希望與人廝守終生！

297
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:17,620
That's how much you wanted to be with someone
你打電話給珍妮絲 這證明你希望與人廝守終生！

298
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,320
You've made it. You're there
你已經改變了！ 你不一樣了！

299
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,680
You are ready to make a commitment
你準備好做出承諾了！

300
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:26,740
Whoa, don't know about that
但是自己卻不知道！

301
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:35,920
Whoa, what you got there?
你拿了什麼？

302
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:38,080
Something else that's not yours that you can break?
不是你的東西 而你想要打破？

303
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:40,740
No
但是自己卻不知道！

304
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,700
I know you like this and I want you to have it
我知道你喜歡這個 我也要你收下它

305
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:47,160
I think it will look good in our apartment

306
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:49,340
Thank you
謝謝

307
00:20:56,540 --> 00:20:57,420
That's fine
沒關係

308
00:20:59,240 --> 00:20:59,680
Hey

309
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:03,240
Well, you will all be pleased to know that I have a date tomorrow night

310
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:07,060
This woman, Allison, from work, she is great
我的同事愛莉森 人很不錯

311
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:08,800
She's pretty. She's smart
她又漂亮又聰明 我一直…

312
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:11,720
And I've been holding off asking her out in the past
沒有約她出來 因為她有一個…

313
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:16,480
because she has a unusually large head
不尋常的大頭！

314
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:19,980
But I'm not going to let that stuff hang me up anymore
但我不要讓這種事情阻止我

315
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:23,000
Look at me. I'm growing
看看我，我成熟了

316
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,720
Hey, you can't recycle yearbooks, can you?
同學錄有沒有回收？

317
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:28,920
I'll take that
那個給我

318
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:30,560
You want his yearbook?
你要他的同學錄？

319
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:33,940
Yeah. Some people said some nice things about him
有人說了他的好話 應該留下來

320
00:21:33,940 --> 00:21:35,060
You think somebody should have it?

321
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:37,360
Oh, gosh, this is so weird
這真的很奇怪

322
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:41,560
I mean, his whole life was in this apartment and now it's gone
他整個生命都在這公寓度過 現在人去樓空

323
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:45,040
You know, I think it would be nice if we just took a few moments
我想我們應該為 哈克先生默哀一會兒

324
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:46,480
from Mr. Heckles

325
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:50,660
I mean, he was kind of a pain. He was
他是個麻煩人物 但他是個人物

326
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:52,160
But he was a person
他是個麻煩人物 但他是個人物

327
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:54,580
What?

328
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:00,020
You're all going to hell
你們全都會下地獄

329
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,500
It's really not that big
其實沒有那麼大！

330
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,060
Taking that with you, huh?
你要拿那個走吧？ 沒錯

331
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:07,660
Oh, yeah
你要拿那個走吧？ 沒錯

332
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:15,920
Hey, you coming?
你來嗎？

333
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:17,740
Yeah, in a second
等一下

334
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:35,300
Goodbye, Mr. Heckles
再見，哈克先生

335
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:40,660
We'll try to keep it down
我們會安靜點

336
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:53,740
Oh, my major was totally useless
我完全學非所用

337
00:22:54,060 --> 00:22:57,180
I mean, how often do you look in the classifieds and see philosopher wanted?
報紙上什麼時候看得到 「徵求哲學家」？

338
00:22:58,180 --> 00:22:58,540
Sure
對啊

339
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:01,260
My God, that's a big head
天啊，那真是個大頭！

340
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:05,640
It didn't look this big in the office
在辦公室看起來沒這麼大 也許是因為燈光

341
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:06,900
Maybe it's the lighting
在辦公室看起來沒這麼大 也許是因為燈光

342
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:10,140
My head must look like a golf ball at work
我的頭在公司 一定像個高爾夫球那麼小

343
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:13,820
All right, don't get hung up on it
不要想了 快列出你喜歡她的五件事

344
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:16,140
Quick, quick, list five things you like about her

345
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:20,280
Nice smile, good dresser, big head, big head, big head
笑容很美，衣著高雅 大頭，大頭，還是大頭！
